 "note": "The northern semiarid kit's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md). leaf.* replace the kit's procedural leaf textures when the page carries this pack (the showcase; a page without it keeps the procedural ones): keep 0 is a grey detail map the species' instance colour colours. bark.* and wood.silver replace the bark buckets' canvases (keep 0 under the species' vertex colours; means() divides the pack's brightness out). ground.* are the showcase host's ground layers (45-host-stage.js), blended per vertex by zone over the painted ground. litter: one cell of card.litter. (2026-10-22, the owner's delivery) leaf.pappus, leaf.stipa: one cell of card.pappus.giant and card.stipa; leaf.fin: card.fin.membrane, a cell cut and turned on its side in 50-species (the frond card runs along +x); seed.samara: one single-winged maple key (card.samara.maple, full colour), the flying helicopter seeds (89c-host-seeds.js); bark.gnarled: bark.saxaul. leaf.tangle: one cell of card.tumble (the tumblers); ground.silt: ground.lakebed.shells, the drained lake's floor with its shells and strand ripples (both delivered 2026-10-22, the last of the kit's prompts). Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/nsemiarid after any change, then python3 build.py. (2026-10-23) the small and weird's skins (keep 0: each species' colour colours them): skin.smooth the bead chains' beads, skin.banded (skin.alien.banded) the sail candelabra's columns, organic.chitin the mace heads' spikes, organic.coil.ribbed the horn pipes; skin.cactus also dresses the striders' barrels and bark.gnarled their stilts and stubs.",
